Local changes to the vendored rdesktop sources:

- utils.c: util_dialog_choice() offers the GUI prompt (xgui_choice_dialog) before
  refusing a non-interactive stdin, so GUI-launched clients can answer
  certificate prompts.
- nettle_compat.h (new, force-included by build.rs): Nettle 4 *_digest()
  signatures for cssp.c and ntlmssp.c.
- rdesktop.c, xwin.c, xkeymap.c, xclip.c, ewmhints.c, xgui.c and rdesktop's rdpsnd
  back-ends are not vendored; their state and functions live in Rust.
- rdesktop.h: the _WIN32 branch uses Winsock 2 (IPv6) and lean Windows headers.
- On Windows, build.rs leaves out addin.c, serial.c, parallel.c,
  printercache.c, lspci.c, ctrl.c and rdpear.c; win32_stubs.c covers what the
  remaining files call in them, and win32_ports.c (new) is serial and parallel
  port redirection for Windows: DeviceIoControl passthrough, reads that return
  at once, and WAIT_ON_MASK completed by polling.
- rdpdr.c: serial and parallel reads and writes complete immediately on Windows.
- printer.c: jobs go through ui_printer_open/write/close (src/printing.rs)
  instead of popen("lpr -P name") through a shell; types.h: PRINTER.job.
- disk.c: Windows shims at the top of the file, and win32/fnmatch.h.
- rdpdr.c: disk reads and writes complete immediately on Windows.
- build.rs renames pkix_asn1_tab, which collides with GnuTLS's table of the same
  name when GnuTLS is linked statically.
- utils.c: the certificate store lives under %USERPROFILE% on Windows.
- tcp.c: TLS also offers TLS 1.0/1.1 and, last, the 3DES and RC4 ciphers unpatched
  Server 2003 needs, where the crypto library still has them.
- rdpsnd.c, rdpsnd_dsp.c: vendored without sound input, with one output driver,
  rdpsnd_vintrdp.c, which plays through src/audio.rs.
- cliprdr.c: cliprdr_send_temp_directory(). Without this message Windows Server
  2003 neither offers nor accepts files on the clipboard.
- rdp.c: the client Input Capability Set advertises INPUT_FLAG_UNICODE, and the
  server's inputFlags are kept in g_server_input_flags, so characters with no
  key behind them can go as Unicode keyboard events where the server takes them.
- utils.c: logger() writes everything to stderr, Notice and Verbose included;
  stdout carries `vintrdp --control` replies.
